<newsitem itemid="397520" id="root" date="1997-02-24" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Persetel raises interim shr, div.</title>
<headline>Persetel raises interim shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended November 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     29.3	   vs	18.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 11.2	   vs	8.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   55.4	   vs	28.8</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   63.8	   vs	38.5</p>
<p>    Tax			 8.1	    vs	8.7</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   14.3	   vs	6.4</p>
<p>    Turnover		  517.1	  vs	403.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     11.0	   vs	3.2 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Persetel Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that in the short term the results of the South African business would be affected negatively by the timing of the completion of certain large contracts and the high interest burden resulting from the high asset level in the PC business.</p>
<p>It said it still remained their intention to provide an compound annual growth rate of more than 35 percent in earnings per share.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
